{
  "_readme": [
    "Adapter-independent ground truth for the UsageSourcePort contract (P1-3).",
    "The in-memory fake and every real adapter's fixtures encode THIS. When an adapter and the",
    "fake disagree, the fake is right and the adapter has a bug.",
    "",
    "All windows are in the CLOSED PAST on purpose. C7 (idempotence) and C8 (window honoured)",
    "are both flaky or vacuous against a window containing 'now': an adapter that ignores the",
    "window and always answers 'today' passes a two-window test whenever the corpus happens to be",
    "today's. Closed-past windows make that adapter fail no matter what day CI runs.",
    "",
    "Money is asserted in INTEGER CENTS. Float sums drift, and C9's '< 1e-9' tolerance hides the",
    "drift instead of catching the re-pricing it is meant to catch."
  ],
  "rows": [
